    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d898">

                <pb facs="0854" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6443.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Nuevo
                            Laredo to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nuevo Laredo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-01T09:00:00-06:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1913—9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Peace commission held harmonious session here yesterday and departed this morning
                    for El Paso via San Antonio. In addition to those named in my February 27, 2 [5]
                    p.m., the following personnel are included in the party: Pasqual Orozco, sr.,
                    Andres Garze Galan, Cristoforo Caballero, José Cordova, Rafael R. Flores,
                    Nicanor Valdez, Indalecio Vara, Juan Garza Galan, and Adolfo Fuentes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
